addresses-method: A and AAAA of every host asked of two resolvers over DoH, certificates checked (dig 9.20
  +https: dns.quad9.net at 9.9.9.9 and cloudflare-dns.com at 1.1.1.1), 13:41 to 13:47 UTC; both gave the same
  answers for every host.
hosting-method: the origin AS of each measured address from RIPEstat network-info (RIS), its holder and seat
  from the registry's RDAP record (RIPE, ARIN, LACNIC); cdn where the address belongs to Fastly (AS54113) or
  Cloudflare (AS13335). crypto.sx's backend sits behind Cloudflare: AS12876 is Scaleway's AS by RDAP, from the
  list's word that Scaleway hosts it, not from a measured address.
configs-method: GET https://HOST/.well-known/odohconfigs at 13:44 UTC and again at 13:54 UTC, same bytes each
  time; every target served one config of 46 bytes: version 1, X25519, HKDF-SHA256, AES-128-GCM.
doh-method: one query (example.com A) to each target operator's plain DoH: Cloudflare and the four dnscry.pt
  nodes answered a POST with application/dns-message; doh.crypto.sx answered a GET and refused a POST (405).
round-trips: a minimal RFC 9230 client from the project's research (odoh_probe.py), python3 -I, public names
  only (example.com, wikipedia.org), from one residential vantage point at 13:46 UTC:
  numa to cloudflare: 6 of 6 answered, first 249 ms, warm median 62 ms;
  crypto-sx-fastly to dnscry-pt-fra01: 6 of 6 answered, first 299 ms, warm median 46 ms;
  the other pairs the rule allows, 2 queries each: numa to crypto-sx, crypto-sx-fastly to dnscry-pt-waw01,
  dnscry-pt-vie01 and dnscry-pt-lis01, all answered.
https-record: the HTTPS record (type 65) of each target host asked of cloudflare-dns.com and dns.quad9.net
  over DoH, the answers decoded for SvcParamKey 32769 (odohconfig, RFC 9230 section 6); both resolvers agreed:
  odoh.cloudflare-dns.com has a DNSSEC-validated HTTPS record with alpn, ipv4hint and ipv6hint only, no
  odohconfig, although Cloudflare's ODoH page (updated 2026-10-02) says the key is published there;
  odoh.crypto.sx has an HTTPS record with alpn, ipv4hint, ech and ipv6hint, no odohconfig;
  fra01, waw01, vie01 and lis01.dnscry.pt are CNAMEs to vpsNNN.brueggus.de with no HTTPS record.
  No target publishes its config in DNS, so there is nothing to compare: /.well-known/odohconfigs is the only
  source, and configs holds that copy.
