rule: a pair is refused when relay and target share an operator, a person, a jurisdiction, or a hosting or CDN
  AS. On these values numa pairs only with cloudflare and crypto-sx (with dnscry.pt it shares DE), and
  crypto-sx-fastly only with the dnscry.pt targets (with cloudflare it shares US, with crypto-sx its person).
  Both default pairs pass.
left-out: the relay sh2o (odoh-relay.sh2o.link): the list says only that it is in Spain and names no operator.
  The targets of Tiarap (odoh-id-gmail, odoh-tiarap.org): they filter ads, trackers and malware. Snowstorm
  (dope.snowstorm.love): no seat of its operator found. The other 121 dnscry.pt targets: one operator and
  person; four nodes on hosts in four countries are enough. Of those looked up, zrh01 (AS51852 of Private
  Layer INC, Panama, on an IPv4 block held by a Hong Kong company) and gva01 (AS204957 of Green Floid LLC, US,
  which would share US with the Fastly relay) were left out.
